---
description: Cryptex security and untrusted-input rules
globs:
  - "**/*.rs"
  - "**/*.ts"
  - "**/*.tsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

Security requirements:
- Treat imported memory, Markdown, attachment metadata and AI output as untrusted input.
- Renderer/webview code must use least privilege.
- UI code must not receive arbitrary shell or filesystem access.
- Secrets belong in OS secure storage.
- Logs must not contain memory bodies, credentials, recovery material or secrets by default.
- Files arriving through synchronization are not trusted merely because they exist locally.
- Purge, recovery and trust-changing operations require the authority defined by the specification.
- Never bypass validation or authorization to simplify implementation.
